# Arithmetic: exact integers, division, rounding, bits, constants and real functions.
mathematics is a calculation-case.
the input of magnitude is -9007199254740993.
the inputs of division is [-7, 3].
the input of rounding is -2.5.
the inputs of extrema is [1000000000000000000001, 1e21].
the inputs of gcd is [-42, 30].
the inputs of bits is [13, 6].
the input of trigonometry is 1.
the radius of circle is 3.

the absolute of ?case is absolute value of ?number if the input of ?case is ?number.

# [quotient toward zero, quotient toward negative infinity, remainder, modulo]
the result of division is [?a quotient ?b, ?a floor quotient ?b, ?a remainder ?b, ?a modulo ?b]
if the inputs of division is [?a, ?b].

# [floor, ceiling, nearest (ties toward positive infinity), truncate, integer part, fractional part]
the result of rounding is [floor of ?number, ceiling of ?number, round of ?number,
truncate of ?number, integer part of ?number, fractional part of ?number]
if the input of rounding is ?number.

the result of extrema is [minimum of ?a with ?b, maximum of ?a with ?b]
if the inputs of extrema is [?a, ?b].
the result of gcd is greatest common divisor of ?a with ?b if the inputs of gcd is [?a, ?b].

# [intersection, union, xor, complement of first input, left shift, right shift]
the result of bits is [bit intersection of ?a with ?b, bit union of ?a with ?b,
bit xor of ?a with ?b, bit complement of ?a, ?a shifted left by 3, ?a shifted right by 3]
if the inputs of bits is [?a, ?b].

the constants of mathematics is [constant pi, constant e] if mathematics is a calculation-case.
the circumference of ?circle is 2 times constant pi times ?radius if the radius of ?circle is ?radius.
the round-trip of trigonometry is tangent of arc tangent of ?number if the input of trigonometry is ?number.

